    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass \u2014 0 failures, 0 errors. The change is complete and green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Unified identifier.** `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` are now a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 e.g. `NSW277D0C08EF9` (region `NSW`, fiscal year `27`, hash `7D0C08EF`, Luhn check digit `9`). The `HASH8` is the same SHA-256-over-`(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` first-8-upper-hex used by the region-and-hash identity, and `CHK` is a single Luhn digit computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n\n**Files touched:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 removed `customerCode` / `membershipNumber` fields+accessors, added `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 new step replacing `AssignCustomerCode` + `AssignMembershipNumber`; computes the memberId and applies collision handling to it (`-<n>` suffix so distinct owners stay distinct).\n- Deleted `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `AssignMembershipNumber.java`, and `CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java` (the standalone `checkDigit` derived from the old customerCode; its Luhn logic now lives inline as the `CHK` segment).\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 collapsed the two steps into one `assignMemberId`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` mapping; `memberId` maps by name.\n- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 audit line and structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` as the primary identifier (customerCode/membershipNumber gone; id, registrationDate, membershipLevel retained).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema entries; added `memberId`. `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) is retained.\n- All four `db/*/schema.sql` \u2014 replaced `customer_code` + `membership_number` columns with `member_id VARCHAR(30)`.\n- Fixed two now-stale `{@link AssignCustomerCode}` javadoc references.\n\nOn the spec's \"the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId\": the fiscal year is embedded in the memberId's `FY` segment (computed from the same registration date), and the audit record/event now reference the memberId. `OwnerSegments` never referenced the old fields \u2014 it derives from membership level and locality \u2014 so nothing there needed changing, and no test asserts otherwise.",
